<title>BELGIUM: EU agrees to apply new world rubber trade pact.</title>
<headline>EU agrees to apply new world rubber trade pact.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union said in a statement that it had agreed to provisionally implement the new International Rubber Agreement from January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>The EU decision, following that of the U.S. and Japan, means that countries representing 77 percent of world rubber imports have agreed to apply the agreement which was concluded in 1995.</p>
<p>This exceeds the 75 per cent of world rubber imports which must be reached under article 61 of the agreement for a new accord to come into force. But ratification by countries representing at least 75 percent of world exporters is also needed.</p>
</text>
